Subject: [PATCH] Introduce BurpeeActor + CompanionActor presentation seam
 (Step 2B-M2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On top of the approved BURPEE_MASTER_APPROVED.png identity master.
Presentation-only: no production art, no raster promotion, no domain,
evaluation, persistence, content, progression or route changes.

- Add src/visual/character/BurpeeActor.tsx: mirrors MaitteActor exactly.
  Callers provide one CompanionActingState; BurpeeActor derives
  character.burpee.<state> itself and forwards that same state to the
  resolved component. BurpeeActorProps has no key/assetKey/petId field, so
  no caller can represent a mismatch between Burpee identity, logical key
  and acting state.
- Add src/visual/character/CompanionActor.tsx: the petId-aware seam a caller
  uses when it only knows "there is a configured companion", not which one
  (docs/narrative/PET-COMPANIONS.md — no pet permanently bound to a
  subject/skill). petId === "burpee" delegates to BurpeeActor; every other
  petId resolves through the existing generic "character.companion" registry
  key, which still wraps CompanionArt unchanged.
- Dependency direction is deliberately bottom-up to avoid a cycle:
  assetRegistry already imports CompanionArt, so CompanionArt must never
  import anything that imports assetRegistry. CompanionArt.tsx is left
  BYTE-FOR-BYTE UNCHANGED — BurpeeActor and CompanionActor never import it
  directly; they only reach it indirectly through getAsset("character.
  companion"). A dedicated static test (dependency-direction.test.ts) checks
  CompanionArt's source text for the four forbidden imports so this can't
  regress silently.
- Add five character.burpee.<state> registry entries (idle, speak, watch,
  success-reaction, retry-reaction), all vectorAsset(BurpeeArt) for now —
  byte-identical output. character.companion is kept, unlike character.
  maitte's bare key removed in Step 2B-M1: it remains the real fallback for
  Pipoca/Will/Lyra, which have no per-state keys yet.
- Migrate ChallengeStageShell's single companion render site from
  <CompanionArt> to <CompanionActor>, preserving petId, petDisplayName, the
  pre-existing "speaking -> speak" override, animated/hydration behaviour,
  positioning and accessibility exactly as before.
- Companion restoration/stolen-color has no model in the current scaffold at
  all (BurpeeArt has no `restored` prop or region gating, unlike Maittê) —
  recorded as PRODUCTION-ASSET-GAP: companion restoration / stolen-color
  contract, blocking any future raster promotion of character.burpee.*, not
  solved here.
- Tests: BurpeeActor key resolution (mocked) + scaffold passthrough
  (unmocked); CompanionActor dispatch (mocked, proves Burpee vs. generic
  fallback routing and prop forwarding) + fallback/Burpee equivalence
  (unmocked, output-identical to calling CompanionArt/BurpeeArt directly);
  ChallengeStageShell companion regression (speaking override, and staying
  petId-agnostic for a non-Burpee pet); dependency-direction static guard.
  99/99 tests passing, typecheck clean, zero new lint violations, zero diff
  under src/game/{domain,evaluation,persistence,state,content},
  src/visual/world-config, src/visual/character/acting.ts and src/routes.

BURPEE_MASTER_APPROVED.png remains an identity/north-star reference only —
not used as a runtime sprite anywhere in this change.

This completes Step 2B-M2 only. Pipoca, Will and Lyra Character Masters,
companion restoration compositing, and Step 2C Overworld composition remain
separate, un-started future work.

